{"audit_findings": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "This ontology demonstrates strong architectural understanding with proper reification patterns and MOA qualifier distinctions. However, it suffers from critical incompleteness: only 8 of the required ~18 D96A INVOIC segment types are modeled. Missing segments include LIN (Line Item), IMD (Item Description), NAD (Name and Address), PAI (Payment Instructions), and CUX (Currencies). The ontology also lacks qualifier-specific distinctions for NAD, DTM, and RFF segments, which are mandatory for D96A compliance.",

  "completeness_score": 0.42,

  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "NameAndAddress (NAD) with qualifier subclasses",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "NAD is MANDATORY in D96A INVOIC. Must have distinct subclasses for NAD+BY (Buyer), NAD+SU (Supplier), NAD+DP (Delivery Party), NAD+IV (Invo", "owl_reviewed_length": 26389, "consultation_logged": true, "audits_remaining": 2}

