{"audit_findings": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "This ontology demonstrates a solid foundational understanding of EDIFACT structure (envelope, segments, composites) and business roles, but suffers from critical **qualifier blindness** and **incomplete segment coverage**. The model defines only 2 segment types (BGM, NAD) when a complete D96A INVOIC requires 15-20. It lacks mandatory segments like DTM (dates with qualifiers), MOA (monetary amounts), LIN (line item), QTY (quantities), PRI (prices), TAX (tax details), and UNS (section separator). The NAD modeling conflates all party types without qualifier distinction, and dates/amounts are modeled as generic classes rather than qualifier-specific instances.",
  "completeness_score": 0.15,
  "extensions_required": [
