{"audit_findings": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "This ontology demonstrates sophisticated OWL modeling with proper use of inverses, disjointness, and restrictions. However, it suffers from critical D96A EANCOM INVOIC incompleteness: only 2 of ~18 required segment types are modeled (BGM, NAD), missing essential elements like line items (LIN), quantities (QTY), monetary amounts (MOA), dates (DTM), taxes (TAX), and references (RFF). The NAD modeling lacks qualifier distinctions (BY/SU/DP are conflated into generic Organization subclasses), and critical EDIFACT structural elements (UNH/UNT message envelope, segment groups, qualifier-based semantics) are absent.",
  "completeness_score": 0.15,
  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "LINSegment (Line Item Segment)",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "Mandatory D96A segment. Each invoice line requires LIN with line number and item identification.", "owl_reviewed_length": 13876, "consultation_logged": true, "audits_remaining": 0}

